JWasm: -Zj makes a JMP to a FAR label short or far, never near

MASM 5 does not make a near JMP to a label of type FAR in the current
segment. A JMP back to one is short if the label is within range and a
far JMP (EAh) otherwise. A forward JMP was sized in pass one, before the
label's type was known, and is left to the forward JMP rule (3 bytes,
EB xx 90 when short). JWasm made both backward cases a near JMP (E9h).

Needed for CHKDSK (CHKPROC.ASM), which jumps to NODDOT, NULLDIRERR and
DDSIZOK, all LABEL FAR.

diff --git a/src/branch.c b/src/branch.c
index acf7588..79b71ad 100644
--- a/src/branch.c
+++ b/src/branch.c
@@ -262,6 +262,16 @@ ret_code process_branch( struct code_info *CodeInfo, unsigned CurrOpnd, const st
     }
 
     if ( state != SYM_EXTERNAL ) {
+        /* -Zj: MASM 5 never makes a near JMP to a FAR label in the current
+         * segment: a JMP back to one is short if it can be, and far
+         * otherwise. A forward JMP was sized in pass one, before the label's
+         * type was known, and is left alone. */
+        if ( Options.masm5_compat && CodeInfo->token == T_JMP &&
+            CodeInfo->mem_type == MT_EMPTY && sym->mem_type == MT_FAR &&
+            opndx->instr != T_SHORT && state == SYM_INTERNAL &&
+            sym->offset < GetCurrOffset() &&
+            (int_32)sym->offset - (int_32)( GetCurrOffset() + 2 ) < SCHAR_MIN )
+            CodeInfo->mem_type = MT_FAR;
         /* v1.94: if a segment override is active,
          check if it's matching the assumed value of CS.
          If no, assume a FAR call.
